  "body": "### Environment\n\n\nNode version: v26.3.0\nnpm version: v11.16.0\nLocal ESLint version: Not found\nGlobal ESLint version: Not found\nOperating System: linux 7.0.0-29-generic\n\n### What parser are you using?\n\nDefault (Espree)\n\n### What did you do?\n\n```js\n/*eslint new-cap: \"error\"*/\n\n// ok\nnew lowerCase()   // reports\nnew UpperCase()  // not reports\n\n// false-negative\nnew toString()  // not reports\nnew constructor()  // not reports\nnew hasOwnProperty()  // and so ...\nnew isPrototypeOf()\nnew propertyIsEnumerable()\nnew valueOf()\nnew toLocaleString()\n```\n\n### What did you expect to happen?\n\n`new toString()` and `new constructor()` alike should be reported.\n\n### What actually happened?\n\nomg, it did not report.\n\n### Link to Minimal Reproducible Example\n\nhttps://eslint.org/play/#\n\n### Participation\n\n- [ ] I am willing to submit a pull request for this issue.\n\n### AI acknowledgment\n\n- [x] I did not use AI to generate this issue report.\n- [ ] (If the above is not checked) I have reviewed the AI-generated content before submitting.\n\n### Additional comments\n\nApparently there is some raw property checks to an object. Prefer `Object.create(null)` or `Object.hasOwn(map, \"key\")`.",
